1) Create the unique adbkey file on your computer (not your router):
$ openssl genpkey -algorithm rsa -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out adbkey

Older OpenSSL versions (e.g. as found on macOS) lack the genpkey command
so use the following shell pipeline:
$ openssl genrsa 2048 | openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -nocrypt -out adbkey

2) Install the created file as /etc/easytether/adbkey on your router:
$ scp adbkey root@192.168.1.1:/etc/easytether/adbkey

3) Make sure the installed file has proper ownership and permissions:
# chown root:root /etc/easytether/adbkey
# chmod 0600 /etc/easytether/adbkey
